# client — Progress (Split 13 rewrite)

Tracks progress converting this package from Check! to Split 13. Tags reflect how much Split-13-specific work each file needs, not whether the current Check! code works.

Legend: [COMPLETE] done for Split 13 (either ported, rewritten, or needed no change) · [IN PROGRESS] being worked on now · [NEEDS WORK] exists, must change/be replaced/repurposed · [MISSING] doesn't exist yet, needs to be created · [WARNING] works but flagged for review · [ERROR] known bug

Updated: 2026-08-31 (session 3). Update this file in the same pass as any change to a listed file.

## Top-level config

- .env.example — [COMPLETE] — infra, game-agnostic.
- .gitignore · components.json · declarations.d.ts · eslint.config.mjs · next.config.ts · postcss.config.mjs · tsconfig.json — [COMPLETE]
- package.json — [NEEDS WORK] — name/description still say "Check!".

## app/

- app/layout.tsx — [WARNING] — compiles and runs, but `next/font/google` fetches Nunito Sans at build time. In any network-restricted environment the production build FAILS on it (dev degrades to a fallback font with a warning). The repo already ships `app/fonts/NunitoSans-{Regular,ExtraBold}.ttf`; switching to `next/font/local` would remove the dependency, but only 400 and 800 exist locally and the UI uses `font-semibold` (57×) and `font-bold` (34×), which would both snap to 800 and flatten the type hierarchy. Left alone deliberately — a decision for the user, not a silent workaround.
- app/providers.tsx — [COMPLETE] — ported. The peek/ability socket bridges and their cleanups are gone; state type renamed.
- app/globals.css — [COMPLETE] for the port — added `--team-a` / `--team-b` tokens (light + dark + `@theme`). Blue vs amber: the safest pair for colour-blind viewers, and neither reads as the red accent. A wider rebrand pass is still open.
- app/page.tsx — [COMPLETE] — copy rewritten for Split 13 (capture/team framing replaces peek/lowest-hand). Not yet committed.
- app/rules/page.tsx — [COMPLETE]. app/rules/{RulesContent,illustrations}.tsx — [COMPLETE] — rewritten for Split 13's rules (capture, stack, teams); the ~63 Check!-specific references (peek/ability/penalty/draw pile) are gone. Not yet committed.
- app/manifest.ts · apple-icon.tsx · icon.svg · icon-512/route.tsx · maskable-icon/route.tsx · opengraph-image.tsx — [COMPLETE] — rebranded (confirmed no "Check" text in any of the five).
- app/robots.ts · sitemap.ts · fonts/ · game/layout.tsx · game/[gameId]/{page,GameClient}.tsx — [COMPLETE]

## components/cards/ (game-agnostic primitives)

- CardAnimationRoot.tsx · CardBack.tsx · CardFlight.tsx · cardRing.ts · PlayingCard.tsx — [COMPLETE] — reused unchanged. `PlayingCard` renders rank over suit glyph, which is exactly what a matching game needs.
- VisualCardStack.tsx — [COMPLETE] — `PublicCard` → `Card` (no face-down cards in Split 13).

## components/game/

- GameBoard.tsx — [COMPLETE] — rebuilt. Four seats with the viewer always at the bottom, partner opposite, opponents left and right (clockwise from your chair is bottom → left → top → right, so the seat that acts after you is on your left). Hosts the team scoreboard, turn timer, table stack, your hand, and the end-of-hand result overlay.
- PlayerHand.tsx — [COMPLETE] — rebuilt. Thirteen cards as an overlapping fan whose rank corners stay visible; a card that would capture is ringed; tap to select, tap again to commit (a card leaves your hand for good, so it takes two deliberate taps).
- PlayerSeat.tsx — [COMPLETE] — NEW, replaces PlayerHandStrip. One opponent/partner: card-back count, name, team, bot/host/disconnected badges, turn highlight. Cannot show faces — the redactor never sends them.
- TableArea.tsx — [COMPLETE] — rebuilt. One capture stack with its live point value and "match a 7 to take it".
- TeamScoreboard.tsx — [COMPLETE] — NEW. Live A vs B, your team marked.
- TurnTimer.tsx — [COMPLETE] — NEW. The 20s clock, shown to everyone, counted against the server's deadline rather than a local countdown so it cannot drift from what the server will actually fire.
- GameLobby.tsx — [COMPLETE] — ported. Four fixed seats in seat order, `hostId`, a solo host against three bots is a legal table, and the status line names how many seats bots will fill.
- GameEventCaption.tsx — [COMPLETE] — ported. Check!'s "final turns" line became a last-lap warning that names what is about to be stranded.
- GameHeader.tsx — [COMPLETE] — wordmark reads "Split 13" with the rebranded BrandMark; the `Check` import is the unrelated lucide checkmark icon used for the copy-link confirmation.
- GameUI.tsx — [COMPLETE] — unchanged; its view switch still holds.
- useGameSounds.ts — [COMPLETE] — rebuilt against Split 13's deltas: throw (stack grows), capture, deal, start, hand over, join/leave, ready/unready, your turn, chat, and a tick in the last 5s of YOUR turn only.
- DELETED (12): AbilityMoment · MatchMoment · PenaltyMoment · CheckMoment · HandGrid · LearnCheckSheet · RoundSummary · ActionController · ActionControllerView · ActionFactories · ActionBarComponent · ActionButton

